## Prose

Write one sentence per line.
Break after the Chinese, Japanese, and Korean full stop `。`, after `！` and `？`, and after the Latin `.`, `!`, and `?`.
A break after a clause, at `、`, `,`, `;`, `:`, or an em dash, may clarify structure.
Never wrap prose to a fixed column, and never join a paragraph onto one line.
Lines have no length limit.
Never use hard line breaks inside a paragraph.
A blank line separates paragraphs.

The rule covers English and Japanese in Markdown files, source-code comments, commit messages, issue and pull request bodies, and release notes.
Consecutive comment lines form a paragraph, and a comment trailing after code stands alone.
When editing a paragraph wrapped to a column, reflow the whole paragraph in the same change.
